  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0122_7c29128e0f9e.png\" style=\"width: 409px; height: 181px;\" /></p><p>Cyclic hemiacetal are formed when an alcohol oxygen atom adds to the carbonyl carbon of an aldehyde or a ketone. Molecules (aldehyde or ketone), which contain both an alcohol and a carbonyl group, can instead undergo an intramolecular reaction to form a cyclic hemiacetal/ hemiketal.</p>"
